knowledge-is-a-lack-of-ignorance-lines-2 = cons "Avik Jain" (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "" (cons "Knowledge is a lack of ignorance" (cons " recovers the Greek definition of truth: *a-lētheia*, un-forgetting, truth defined as the negation of concealment. *Ignorance* (*in-* + *gnarus*, not-knowing) shares the Indo-European root *\*ǵneh₃-* with *knowledge* and Greek *gnōsis*. Defining knowledge as the absence of ignorance recognizes unobstructed knowing as the ground state and ignorance as the artificial partition added atop it — which is why carving inquiry into walled academic fields is an ignorance-generating process." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "*Domain* records the same history in Latin: *dominium*, lordship and private property, from *dominus*, master of an estate. An academic domain is a fenced estate whose occupants agree not to look past its boundary." (cons "" (cons "**The divisions the primitive removes.** Hyperactivity's primitive is identity as paths under computational univalence. An academic cut is merely a projection onto a chosen observation; transport carries structure across equivalent representations, and what any projection forgets is measured exactly by its fiber. From that single primitive, thirteen entrenched disciplinary divisions dissolve:" (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "- **Logic | mathematics | computer science.** Proofs are programs, propositions are types, and the verifier is itself a term of the language: " (cons "proving" (cons " and " (cons "programming" (cons " are one act." nil)))))) (cons "- **Discrete | continuous mathematics.** Cubical intervals and higher cubes supply continuous homotopy geometry that computes directly: discrete combinatorial boundary identities and continuous differential-form Stokes theorems cease to be separate subjects." (cons "- **The systems subfields.** Operating systems, programming languages, compilers, databases, networking, security, and formal verification collapse into one substrate: the OS is a language, storage is content-addressed, networking is peer exchange across ports, compilation is proof-carrying partial evaluation, and security and correctness are one invariant." (cons "- **Hardware | software.** Instruction sets and relaxed memory models (such as x86-TSO) are ordinary definitions inside the language, and emitted machine code carries an explicit simulation relation to its source." (cons "- **Symbolic AI | statistical learning.** Exact context-fiber selection and middle-out structural factoring yield efficient deterministic algorithms for reasoning over raw unstructured records — occupying the exact ground split apart by brittle hand-coded ontologies and opaque weight fitting." (cons "- **Linguistics | computer science | philosophy of meaning.** Hyperactivity is a language of languages: object identity is content just as meaning is invariant to surface spelling, and a name's binding log in the store is literally its etymology." (cons "- **Biology | neuroscience | computation.** Compositional symbolic nervous systems, DNA as an autocatalytic content record, and Lafont interaction agents share one formal dynamics, grounding theoretical neuroscience with end-to-end explanatory reach." (cons "- **Human–computer interaction | theory.** Defining human–computer interaction as the extension of consciousness by tools makes interface architecture a theorem of observation fibers rather than subjective UI taste." (cons (quoted (cons "- **Ethics | political philosophy | engineering.** " (cons "Safety" (cons " unifies program correctness and value alignment (`SafeAt` over observation fibers), turning agency, decentralization, and non-coercive interaction into checkable structural properties." nil)))) (cons "- **Psychiatry | philosophy of mind | sociology.** Normative herd conformity, pathologized cognitive variance, and standpoint relativity are analyzed inside one formal account of observation and boundary compatibility rather than split across clinical and social silos." (cons "- **Sociology | media studies | computing.** Every navigation and exchange over shared content-addressed knowledge is already interpersonal computing." (cons "- **Pure | applied.** Every theorem is an executable construction, and every executable construction carries its proof." (cons "- **The humanities | the sciences.** *Text* and *technology* descend from the same root (*\*teḱs-*, to weave), and historical philology and computational provenance become the same operation inside the store." (cons "" (cons "Every disciplinary wall treated a contingent cut as ontological. Here none is primary: any projection may still be taken when useful, with an exact proof of what it preserves and what its fiber leaves unseen." nil))))))))))))))))))))))
